I'm rather fond of Gugs, myself. Not the toughest or meanest monster by
any standard, but plenty tough and mean enough. Also:
- They have a neat paralysis attack, that can freeze up monsters long
enough for you to finish them off/ run away/ let your other pets get a
bite in.
- They eat all kinds of corpses, helping to leave a nice tidy dungeon
for you, and making them easier to keep tame.
- They can wear armour and use weapons.
- They're easy to pick up. Just learn the "command undead" spell and
wait for your friendly neighbourhood purple L to summon in some
"mosters from beyond the grave".

Note that if you want to wish for a Gug you'd be better wishing for a
spellbook of CU than for a figurine.



